// A must-reject leak that was the family's (soak nov26a, function-bound): a
// seq gathers a call's arguments into one value and selects over it, and a
// `never()` among them makes that no value, so nothing reaches the callee
// and its `Function` bound is asked of nothing. The same call outside a seq
// is refused "i64 must be Function here".
// Expected trace (both engines): 0.
{ let step = seq { 1; { let qf = queuefn(#trigger: never(), 1); qf(7) } }; 0 }
